# /etc/inittab - busybox init stays pid 1; OpenRC runs the runlevels.
# (Alpine Linux boots exactly this way.) Buildroot only installs busybox's
# stock inittab under BR2_INIT_BUSYBOX, so with BR2_INIT_OPENRC this overlay
# owns the file.
#
# The stock inittab's sysinit lines (mount /proc, mount -a, hostname, /dev
# symlinks...) are not replicated here: OpenRC's sysinit and boot runlevels
# (init.sh, localmount, hostname, bootmisc) cover all of them, and localmount
# honours the "ro" root entry in /etc/fstab, keeping the rootfs read-only.
# udev also starts in the sysinit runlevel (udev-gentoo-scripts), so device
# symlinks exist before the default runlevel's sysv-rcs runs /etc/init.d/S??*.
::sysinit:/sbin/openrc sysinit
::sysinit:/sbin/openrc boot
::wait:/sbin/openrc default

# autologin the default user on tty1, the VT sway runs on (previously
# appended to busybox's inittab by post-build.sh).
tty1::respawn:/sbin/getty -n -l /usr/bin/autologin -L tty1 0 linux

# The serial console is not listed here: OpenRC's agetty.<port> service in
# the default runlevel provides it (from BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_GETTY_PORT).

::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot

# "openrc shutdown" stops the default runlevel's services - including
# sysv-rcs, which runs the /etc/init.d/S??* stop actions in reverse order,
# so S15data unmounts /data, /home and /boot. The umount sweeps up the rest.
::shutdown:/sbin/openrc shutdown
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
